+# FY2026 SP-40 valve-seat sourcing award
+
+Prepared for the sourcing steering committee. All figures in US dollars at the mandated FY2026 planning rates, for the full contract year 1 January – 31 December 2026.
+
+## Recommendation
+
+Award the full FY2026 SP-40 volume to **Meridian Precision Works, LLC (SUP-1042)**, contracting **495,010 pieces** for the contract year.
+
+Its FY2026 total cost to Cadence is **USD 959812.87**, which is **USD 2322.53 lower over the contract year** than the second-ranked offer from Brackenridge Tooling Ltd (SUP-4077, USD 962135.40). On a cost-per-good-unit basis that is USD 1.9749 against USD 1.9797, a 0.24% advantage.
+
+This is a single-supplier award for the full contract-year volume, as directed.
+
+## Cost Comparison
+
+The FY2026 good-unit requirement worked to is **486,000 SP-40 pieces** — the twelve monthly SP-40 rows of the frozen November S&OP cycle. The cube dump's October cycle, its `TOTAL` subtotal rows and all SP-22 rows are excluded; SP-22 is the FM-90 orifice plate and is sourced separately.
+
